  "methodology_notes": [
    "Primary target is the unconditional fraction of the next 4 calendar weeks that a currently benched player starts for the same team. Leaving the roster counts as zero future lineup use, which matches Team Utility's roster-fit purpose.",
    "Any-start probability is reported as an upper-bound style usage metric; it gives full credit if the player starts at least once and therefore should not be substituted directly for w.",
    "Conditional start share when still present is diagnostic only because conditioning away cuts/trades overstates the team's retained utility from the original bench asset.",
    "Bootstrap resamples whole team-season clusters, not individual player-weeks, to preserve within-roster dependence."
  ],
  "production_formula": "TeamUtility = (1-w)*lineupDelta_FV + w*benchDelta_FV",
